 Recently there was a debate as to whether you could stone the wizard 
after he stole the amulet, grab his statue and level teleport. I believe 
the verdict was that you couldn't as artifacts don't stay in the statue. 
At the same time I proposed the theory of letting him steal the amulet 
then level teleporting and killing him when he followed. At first I tried 
droppping the amulet and walking away since the wizard collects the bell, 
candleabrum and book of the dead if they are on the level. For some 
reason he wouldn't pick it up. So then I picked it up and waited till he 
stole it. Then I level teleported to level 1. The wizard failed to put in 
an appearance. I can only guess that either a) the wizard does not want to 
chase you from level to level if you has the amulet b) He can't level 
teleport since he has the amulet or c) He knows you need the amulet and 
is waiting for you to come back.

 Other things I've noticed are that killing him with Stormbringer will 
drain his levels so that eating his corpse will not give you teleport 
control. I also found Frostbrand in Moloch's sanctum but once when I 
wielded it I got blasted. The old spoiler lists Frostbrand as neutral 
where I am a chaotic elf. Also when I killed the wizard once on his 
corpse I found - 2 Amulets of Yendor. It did turn out one was a cheap 
plastic version but it's still a rare thing to find.
 BTW does angering peaceful monsters with Stormbringer much your god 
unhappy ? I killed dozens of them in Genholm but when I exited and prayed 
my god was pleased as anything with me.

